<img alt="ad" src="//r2.rev.iq/wowhead.com/House_BlizzGear_Collectables_728x90.webp"/></a></div></div></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Blood Death Knight Trinkets</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by what it is that you and your raid need. A Stamina trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> will make you the least likely to die, especially in a 25-player raiding environment, while a trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> will offer avoidance through the high Strength-to-Parry conversion, with some damage and active mitigation through the Haste. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> - While Strength and Haste look like offensive stats, this offers the best of both worlds, bringing damage through Strength and Haste, while offering defensive utility through the Strength-to-Parry conversion and faster Rune regeneration from the Haste. A super solid trinket, but it has a long internal cooldown (ICD) and can proc at inopportune moments.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a> - Passive Strength with an on-use Haste effect. A solid trinket, but pretty much equivalent to all the trinkets on this list. Only recommended to pick up this trinket if you don't need other gear available through the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> vendors.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> - This trinket brings less defensive utility than the other options on this list, but has a very strong 30-sec proc, which translates into a lot of damage during your opener with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>. Has a long ICD, so may not be worth using on some fights.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> - Offers <b>a lot</b> of avoidance through the Strength-to-Parry conversion and is your best offensive trinket in fights where you don't get super high Vengeance. It's a very expensive trinket to purchase, so don't feel bad about missing out on it, especially if you're raiding in a 25-player environment.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87496/daelos-final-words">
<img alt="Daelo's Final Words" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Daelo's Final Words</span></a> - Offers a surprising amount of Strength while giving a lot of Hit. A very strong option while gearing up. Lines up perfectly with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> - Slightly worse than the alternatives above but offers solid offensive and defensive utility while being easy to obtain.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a> - Can be socketed with any stat of your choosing through Tinker's Gear sockets, like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77544/flashing-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Flashing Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashing Tinker's Gear</span></a>. Shares Tinker's Gear slots with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> if you're an Engineer. Offers more static stats than any other trinket in the game but lacks a meaningful proc or use effect.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> - This is your best defensive trinket by far. The 8871 Dodge also translates into solid offensive utility. Like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a>, this trinket will be quite expensive, but less so than the alternative.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81243/iron-protector-talisman">
<img alt="Iron Protector Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Protector Talisman</span></a> - Like the above option, the Stamina makes it a strong defensive trinket while offering small offensive utility through the Dodge proc effect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86881/stuff-of-nightmares">
<img alt="Stuff of Nightmares" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stuff of Nightmares</span></a> - This trinket offers less defensive utility than the Stamina counterparts, but it does bring more offensive utility.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86790/vial-of-dragons-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Dragon's Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Dragon's Blood</span></a> - Similar to the above alternative, just worse.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89079/lao-chins-liquid-courage">
<img alt="Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage</span></a> - This trinket has similar defensive utility to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a>, but it only offers defensive utility. Not recommended other than for specific purposes, like when tanking <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=60999/sha-of-fear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sha of Fear</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Blood Death Knights</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 7.5% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed. In terms of actual rating, you need <b>2550 Hit</b> and <b>2550 Expertise</b> to reach these caps before accounting for racial bonuses.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might. <br/>
<br/>Reaching 7.5% Hit, otherwise referred to as the "Hit cap," will not guarantee that your spells, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108196/death-siphon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_deathsiphon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Siphon</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a> will land. For that, you'll need Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. A lot of bosses have mechanics that make them unable to parry. Important spells, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49998/death-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_butcher2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Strike</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=62036/rune-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_darkconviction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rune Strike</span></a>, cannot be parried, so reaching 15% Expertise to reach the "hard cap" becomes quite unnecessary. <br/>
<br/>For classes with spells like the Death Knight, reaching this 7.5% number will guarantee your spells land.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Blood Death Knight</span></h2>Your gems will alternate depending on what you and your raid prioritize. We generally have 3 different playstyles (<i>Offensive</i>, <i>Balanced</i>, and <i>Defensive</i>), and below you'll find the appropriate gems for each playstyle. We generally opt to socket for the socket bonus, but if the bonus does not offer an attractive bonus, then opt for the<b> main gem</b> of each category. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Offensive: </b>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76697/smooth-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Smooth Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Sun's Radiance</span></a> (<b>main</b>)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76659/crafty-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Crafty Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crafty Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Green Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76641/piercing-wild-jade">
<img alt="Piercing Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Piercing Wild Jade</span></a></div></li></ul>
<b>Balanced: </b>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76695/flashing-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Flashing Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashing Primordial Ruby</span></a> (<b>main</b>)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76683/retaliating-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Retaliating Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Retaliating Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76664/stalwart-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Stalwart Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stalwart Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li></ul>
